{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779329029,"nonce":"NNWnBbvW1rqkKCoPxmgbpVOY3q8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABC7EYUA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149","origin":"github"},"title":"Deployment 2026-05-21: validate small-wins PRs + udp_bridge WARN demote + FCU EK3 Z-source reconfig","message":"## Operators\n\n- Roland + Claude Code Agent\n\n## Hosts in use\n\n- **gabby** — boat-side Linux / ROS host (data hub + boat compute)\n- **mercat** — boat-side Windows / QINSy host (if a survey phase is reached)\n- **salmon** — operator station\n- Field agents as needed.\n\n## Scope\n\nValidate the small-wins batch (currently draft PRs, **must land before launch**)\nplus the now-merged `udp_bridge#24` WARN demote, in a single short deployment.\n\n### Prerequisites — MUST be merged before launch\n\n- [#146](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/146) — Remove `diagnostic_aggregator` from operator launches (closes #141)\n- [#147](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/147) — `output='both'` in BizzyBoat launches (closes #139)\n- [#148](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/148) — Remove stale `bencloud` ping target (closes #140)\n- [`rolker/ros2_network_monitor#24`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/pull/24) — `mikrotik_monitor` + `teltonika_monitor` startup-connect hardening (closes ros2_network_monitor#23)\n\n### Already merged — also under test this deployment\n\n- [`rolker/udp_bridge#24`](https://github.com/rolker/udp_bridge/pull/24) — WARN-log noise demote + per-remote `DiagnosticStatus` (closes udp_bridge#22). Merged 2026-05-21.\n\n## Validation plan — per PR\n\n| PR | What to check | Pass criteria |\n|---|---|---|\n| #146 (remove aggregator) | Operator UI on salmon during ops | Annunciator still shows real-time diagnostics from `/diagnostics`. No STALE `/Operator/*` buckets (because no aggregator). `/diagnostics_agg` topic absent (`ros2 topic list \\| grep diag` confirms). |\n| #147 (`output='both'`) | After mission, check launch log files for any node that crashed or printed errors | Crash output + ERROR logs present in `~/.ros/log/\u003csession\u003e/` for the four touched launches. (Pre-flight: intentionally kill one node mid-launch to confirm crash output lands in the log file, not just the terminal.) |\n| #148 (remove bencloud) | Operator-side ping_monitor diagnostic during ops | No `bencloud` key in `Ping: ping.op:` `DiagnosticStatus` KVs. Toplevel ping rollup is not permanently red from a dead target. |\n| `ros2_network_monitor#24` (startup hardening) | Operator-side and boat-side monitors with **device unreachable at startup** (e.g. boat router off) | Both monitors stay alive (no silent process death). `DiagnosticStatus` publishes at level `ERROR` with message containing `(attempt N, retry in Xs)`. Operator panel shows progress, not silence. Once the device comes up, monitors resume normal polling. |\n| `udp_bridge#24` (WARN demote) | Operator-side `/rosout` + bag during a lossy phase (e.g. brief Starlink-only at distance) | Per-event `Giving up on resend` WARN volume dramatically reduced (target: orders of magnitude vs the 27,992 entries / ~2h baseline from 2026-05-19). Per-remote `DiagnosticStatus` shows give-up rate. |\n\n## Stretch goals (only if time allows and prerequisites met)\n\n- **`#138` FCU reconfig validation** — bench-stage the `EK3_SRC1_POSZ=3` + `EK3_GPS_OFFS` + `GPS_POS1_X/Y/Z` params; if applied before this deployment, verify `mavros/global_position/*` reports at `base_link` and `sea_surface_estimator` produces sane water-level estimates. (Roadmap §Both nav at base_link.)\n- **`#130` OTH field validation** — if conditions permit, take the boat past direct comms range on Starlink-only and run a short autonomous trackline. (Roadmap §Over-horizon.)\n- **Topic-budget cull measurement** — record a Starlink-only segment for the bandwidth/saturation analysis the roadmap calls for. (Roadmap §Over-horizon \"Must finish before June 4\".)\n\n## Carry-forward items to keep in mind\n\n- **RC mode-switch at fringe range** — FCU honors RC channel even with `FS_THR_ENABLE=0`. Pin RC mode switch to AUTO/GUIDED or power off the controller before autonomous segments.\n- **BT `SkipUnknownTaskType` catchall** — [`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#25`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/issues/25) filed but not yet fixed; a survey-line abort silently marks the line done. Be alert for hover-and-quit.\n- **mavros `/global` Z drift** — known ~5 m/hour drift without the #138 reconfig; chart-datum chain remains on the field-revert workaround until #138 lands.\n\n## Wrap-up\n\nPer the workspace per-deployment convention:\n- Per-host logs at `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-XX_\u003chost\u003e_logs.md`\n- One wrap-up PR closing this issue\n- Roadmap §Class-day operator observability \"small easy wins\" bullets check off four of five entries once this deployment validates them\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}